# Cursor AI Rules for this Repository

## Project Context
- This project is a personal finance task management app.
- The app focuses on executing monthly money-related tasks (transfers, withdrawals, payments).
- It is NOT a traditional expense tracking or accounting app.
- Budget sessions are based on payday cycles.

## Tech Stack (Strict)
- Frontend: Next.js (App Router)
- Backend: Firebase (Firestore, Auth)
- Language: TypeScript
- Styling: Minimal (CSS Modules or Tailwind if already present)
- State management: React hooks / simple context only

❗ Do NOT introduce other frameworks, databases, or state management libraries without explicit instruction.

## Architecture Rules
- Follow a simple layered structure:
  - UI (components)
  - ViewModel / Logic (hooks or services)
  - Data access (Firebase repositories)
- Keep logic out of UI components as much as possible.
- Avoid over-engineering (no DDD, no Clean Architecture unless requested).

## Data & Domain Rules
- BudgetSession is the core domain unit (monthly cycle).
- Tasks represent executable money actions.
- Account balances are updated ONLY when a task is marked as completed.
- Never auto-sync with banks or external services.

## Coding Rules
- Prioritize readability over cleverness.
- Prefer explicit logic over abstractions.
- Avoid premature optimization.
- Use clear naming aligned with the domain (Account, Task, BudgetSession).

## MVP Scope Control
- Implement only what is defined as "Must" in the requirements.
- Features marked as "Nice to Have" should be ignored unless explicitly requested.
- If a feature is unclear, ask for clarification instead of guessing.

## UI Rules
- Favor simple list-based UI.
- No complex animations.
- One primary action per screen.
- Desktop-first, but responsive.

## AI Behavior Rules
- Do not invent new features.
- Do not change the tech stack.
- Do not refactor unrelated code.
- When assumptions are necessary, clearly mark them with comments (e.g. // assumption).

